<title>JAPAN: Japan buying of US, EU car parts seen rising--JAMA.</title>
<headline>Japan buying of US, EU car parts seen rising--JAMA.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japan Automobile Manufacturers' Association (JAMA) said on Thursday that it expects Japan's purchases of U.S.- and E.U.-made car parts to increase further in the current business year to March 31, 1998.  </p>
<p>Asked if such purchases would rise, the official said:</p>
<p>&quot;Japan's purchases of U.S.- and EU-made car parts are likely to increase in view of rising production by Japanese car makers in the United States and Europe and the increase in the variety of product lines.&quot;</p>
</text>
